{"type":"assistant_message","payload":{"text":"> I read this as Implementation - Implement Ferryx app badge synchronization with `cmd_notification_set_badge_count`, bind it to `state.unreadTabIds` lifecycle in `App.tsx`, and verify focused tests.\n\n### Summary of Edits\n\n1. **Native DTO & Types (`ui/src/lib/types.ts`)**:\n   - Added `NotificationBadgeResult` and alias `SetBadgeCountResult`:\n     ```ts\n     export interface NotificationBadgeResult {\n       readonly supported: boolean;\n       readonly count: number;\n       readonly badgeLabel?: string;\n     }\n     ```\n\n2. **IPC Wrapper & Normalization (`ui/src/lib/tauri.ts`)**:\n   - Added `normalizeBadgeCount(count: number): number` ensuring finite numbers clamped to `0..0xFFFF_FFFF`.\n   - Added `setBadgeCount(count: number): Promise<SetBadgeCountResult>` calling native `cmd_notification_set_badge_count`.\n\n3. **App Lifecycle Synchronization (`ui/src/App.tsx`)**:\n   - Derived `unreadBadgeCount` from `Object.values(state.unreadTabIds ?? {}).filter(Boolean).length` (single source of truth).\n   - Hooked up `useEffect(() => { void setBadgeCount(unreadBadgeCount).catch(reportRuntimeError); }, [reportRuntimeError, unreadBadgeCount])` to sync on startup, restore, mark-unread, and clear-unread while propagating native errors to `reportRuntimeError`.\n\n4. **Test Suite Coverage (`ui/src/lib/tauri.test.ts`, `ui/src/App.test.tsx`)**:\n   - Verified typed IPC invocation, payload formatting, boundary value normalization, non-tauri fallback, and runtime error propagation.\n\n---\n\n### Rust Integration Contract\n\n- **Command Name**: `cmd_notification_set_badge_count`\n- **Request Payload**: `{ count: number }` (Rust `count: u32`)\n- **Result Schema**: `{ supported: boolean, count: number, badgeLabel?: string }`"}}
